import itertools
S={(0,0),(0,1),(0,-1),(1,0),(-1,0),(0,2),(0,-2),(2,0),(-2,0),(1,1),(1,-1),(-1,1),(-1,-1)}

def covers(center, cell):
    cr,cc=center; r,c=cell
    return (r-cr,c-cc) in S

def occupies(center, cell):
    return covers(center, cell)

hole=(0,0)
ring=[(-1,0),(1,0),(0,-1),(0,1)]
# candidate centers in box [-6,6]"'^2 that cover at least one ring cell but not hole
cand=[]
for cr in range(-6,7):
  for cc in range(-6,7):
    if occupies((cr,cc), hole):
      continue
    covered=[p for p in ring if occupies((cr,cc), p)]
    if covered:
      cand.append(((cr,cc),tuple(covered)))
print('"'cand',len(cand))
# choose up to 5 centers pairwise non-overlap in bbox sense? approximate use no shared occupied cells on local area [-8,8]
def motif_cells(center):
  cr,cc=center
  return {(cr+dr,cc+dc) for dr,dc in S}

for k in range(3,6):
  for combo in itertools.combinations(cand,k):
    centers=[x[0] for x in combo]
    cells=[motif_cells(c) for c in centers]
    ok=True
    for i in range(k):
      for j in range(i+1,k):
        if cells[i]&cells[j]: ok=False
    if not ok: continue
    # ring covered?
    union=set().union(*cells)
    if all(p in union for p in ring) and hole not in union:
      # how many motifs adjacent to hole?
      adj=set()
      for idx,cellset in enumerate(cells):
        if any(p in cellset for p in ring): adj.add(idx)
      print('found',k,centers,[combo[i][1] for i in range(k)],'K',len(adj))
      raise SystemExit
print('none')
