import itertools, math
S={(0,0),(0,1),(0,-1),(1,0),(-1,0),(0,2),(0,-2),(2,0),(-2,0),(1,1),(1,-1),(-1,1),(-1,-1)}

def motif_cells(center):
  cr,cc=center
  return {(cr+dr,cc+dc) for dr,dc in S}

def analyze(centers, holes):
  sets=[motif_cells(c) for c in centers]
  # nonoverlap
  for i in range(len(sets)):
    for j in range(i+1,len(sets)):
      if sets[i] & sets[j]: return None
  out=[]
  union=set().union(*sets)
  for h in holes:
    ring=[(h[0]-1,h[1]),(h[0]+1,h[1]),(h[0],h[1]-1),(h[0],h[1]+1)]
    if h in union or not all(p in union for p in ring):
      return None
    adj=[i for i,s in enumerate(sets) if any(p in s for p in ring)]
    ds=sorted(((centers[i][0]-h[0])**2+(centers[i][1]-h[1])**2, i) for i in range(len(centers)))
    out.append((h,len(adj),adj,ds[:2]))
  return out

holes=[(0,0),(0,4)]
# candidate centers in local box not occupying holes and within 2 of ring cells or as selector nearby
cand=[]
for cr in range(-8,9):
  for cc in range(-8,13):
    cells=motif_cells((cr,cc))
    if any(h in cells for h in holes):
      continue
    # keep centers within moderate radius to influence nearest distances
    # require either cover at least one ring cell or be within dist"'^2 <= 10 of some hole
    covers=False
    for h in holes:
      ring=[(h[0]-1,h[1]),(h[0]+1,h[1]),(h[0],h[1]-1),(h[0],h[1]+1)]
      if any(p in cells for p in ring): covers=True
    near=min((cr-h[0])**2+(cc-h[1])**2 for h in holes) <= 10
    if covers or near:
      cand.append((cr,cc))
print('"'cand',len(cand))
for combo in itertools.combinations(cand,5):
  res=analyze(combo,holes)
  if not res: continue
  if {k%2 for _,k,_,_ in res}"'!={0,1}: continue
  if not all(ds[0][0] < ds[1][0] for *_,ds in res): continue
  print('"'found',combo,res)
  raise SystemExit
print('none')
